# AxonFlow Git Attributes

# Exclude session notes from git archives
# This prevents CLAUDE.md from being included in release tarballs
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
CLAUDE*.md export-ignore
**/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
**/CLAUDE*.md export-ignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The runtime-e2e suite ledger is APPEND-ONLY, so every pair of concurrent
# lanes conflicts on it by construction (#3722).
#
# Each lane that adds a suite appends one row at the end of a 369-line file.
# Two such branches always produce `CONFLICT (content)` on the same final
# hunk, and the cost is not the rebase: a conflicted PR is DIRTY, and a dirty
# PR runs NO CI at all - its check list is EMPTY rather than red, which is
# indistinguishable from a clean board under any readiness check that scores
# "nothing failing and nothing pending". So each merge silently zeroes the
# evidence for every open sibling.
#
# `merge=union` removes the class permanently for this file and ONLY this
# file, because it is the one place where the correct resolution is always
# "keep both rows" - the ledger is a set of independent suite declarations,
# not a document with an order that means anything. It is deliberately NOT
# applied to CHANGELOG.md, where union glues a section's closing line onto the
# following bullet (measured three times on this train) and where the
# resolution genuinely depends on which edition heading an entry belongs
# under.
#
# WHAT UNION CAN STILL GET WRONG, and what catches it. Union concatenates both
# sides of the hunk verbatim; if either side lacked a trailing newline the two
# rows are glued into ONE line carrying more than four tab-separated fields.
# The ledger loader in scripts/e2e/lint-runtime-e2e-executors.sh reads fields
# with `cut -f1..4`, which returns the FOURTH of however many there are and
# reports the row as well-formed - so union without a field-COUNT check trades
# a loud conflict for a silent malformed row. Measured, not argued: appending a
# fifth field to a real row left that loader at rc=0 with the row's note
# silently truncated, and at rc=1 with the NF!=4 assertion this change adds to
# the same loader. It runs in CI on every PR.
#
# The loader's own bijection check catches SOME glue shapes by accident - a
# suite name swallowed into a note leaves its directory without a row - but it
# reports "no ledger row", which sends the reader after a missing suite rather
# than after the merge that ate one, and it sees nothing at all when the
# swallowed row is in the legitimate row-before-directory window.
#
# Union also cannot merge two edits to the SAME row (it keeps both copies,
# which the loader's duplicate-suite check then rejects) - the loud outcome,
# which is correct for the one case where a human really must choose.
scripts/e2e/runtime_e2e_suites.tsv merge=union
